  " <!DOCTYPE html>\n\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"/>\n<meta content=\"Parckwart\" name=\"author\"/>\n<meta content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" name=\"viewport\"/>\n<link href=\"/favicon.ico\" rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/vnd.microsoft.icon\"/>\n<style>\n\t\t\t\tbody {\n\t\t\t\t\tfont-family: sans-serif;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\n\tbody {\n\t\tmax-width: 1200px;\n\t\tmargin: auto;\n\t\tpadding: 10px;\n\t}\n\t\n\t#rss-link {\n\t\ttext-decoration: none;\n\t}\n\t\n\ttable, td, td {\n\t\tfont-size: 13px;\n\t\tborder: 1px solid black;\n\t\tborder-collapse: collapse;\n\t\tpadding: 5px;\n\t\tword-break: break-all;\n\t}\n\t\n\ttd.description {\n\t\tfont-weight: bold;\n\t}\n\t\n\tli {\n\t\tmargin: 10px 0;\n\t}\n\n</style>\n<meta content=\"index, follow, archive\" name=\"robots\"/>\n<title>Parckwart’s Website</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Welcome to my website!</h1>\n<table>\n<tr><td class=\"description\">Normal Internet</td><td>\n<a href=\"https://www.parckwart.de/\">www.parckwart.de</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"description\">Tor Onion Service Version 2</td><td>\n<a href=\"http://parckwartvo7fskp.onion/\">parckwartvo7fskp.onion</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"description\">Tor Onion Service Version 3</td><td>\n<b>45tbhx5prlejzjgn36nqaxqb6qnm73pbohuvqkpxz2zowh57bxqawkid.onion</b>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<address>\n\t\tEmail: mail <b>at</b> parckwart <b>dot</b> de <small><a href=\"/pgp_key\">(PGP key)</a></small>\n</address>\n<br/>\n<a href=\"/imprint\">Imprint</a>\n<p>\n<b>Disclaimer: </b>Some of my friends and family have email accounts in the <i>parckwart.de</i> domain. Any email that doesn’t originate from the above address was <strong>not</strong> sent by me.\n\t</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>\n\t\tThis is my personal website where I collect some ideas of mine. The views expressed are nothing but my own views.\n\t</p>\n<p>\n\t\tWhoever may wish to contact me can do so via email, preferably using PGP encryption. I despise the use of large, centralized networks run by profit-oriented companies, such as Facebook or Twitter, which will sell one’s data and violate one’s human rights for profit in the current economic landscape. Additionally, one has to worry about surveillance of their communications by state agencies, which are just as determined to violate one’s privacy as corporations are. It is best practice to trust neither one of them and educate yourself in privacy-protecting technologies.\n\t</p>\n<h2 id=\"computer_stuff\">Computer Stuff</h2>\n<p>\n\t\tI run a few <a href=\"http://rougmnvswfsmd4dq.onion/rs.html#search/parckwart\">relays</a> for the <a href=\"http://expyuzz4wqqyqhjn.onion/about/overview.html.en\">Tor network</a>.\n\t</p>\n<h3>Articles</h3>\n<a href=\"/rss/computer_stuff.xml\" id=\"rss-link\">\n<img alt=\"Feed Icon\" src=\"/files/rss.png\"/>\n\t\tRSS Feed\n\t</a>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/description_json_is_not_a_good_idea\">description.json is not a good Idea</a>\n<i>October 21, 2017</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/tor2web_is_a_mess\">Tor2web is a Mess</a>\n<i>February 28, 2017</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/tracking_browser_window_size_using_css\">Tracking Browser Window Size Using CSS</a>\n<i>January 12, 2017</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/lenovo_thinkserver_fixing_way_too_loud_fans\">Lenovo ThinkServer: Fixing way too Loud Fans</a>\n<i>December 24, 2016</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/bash_and_cgi_parsing_get_and_post_requests\">Bash and CGI: Parsing GET and POST Requests</a>\n<i>June 16, 2016</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/domain_fronting_explained\">Domain Fronting Explained</a>\n<i>May 16, 2016</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/vnc_remote_support_via_tor_onion_services\">VNC Remote Support via Tor Onion Services</a>\n<i>May 10, 2016</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/firefox_tracking_protection_also_in_normal_mode\">Firefox Tracking Protection also in Normal Mode</a>\n<i>December 6, 2015 </i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/surfing_onion_services_with_firefox\">Surfing Onion Services with Firefox</a>\n<i>October 11, 2015</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/ssh_server_as_tor_onion_service\">SSH Server as Tor Onion Service</a>\n<i>October 11, 2015</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/music_streams_in_tor\">Music Streams in Tor</a>\n<i>October 11, 2015</i>\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"/computer_stuff/apache_http_server_disable_server-status_at_onion_services\">Apache HTTP Server: Disable server-status at Onion Services</a>\n<i>October 11, 2015</i>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Miscellaneous</h2>\n<p>More to come… one day!</p>\n</p></body>\n</html>\n",
  "Parckwart’s Website",
  "http://45tbhx5prlejzjgn36nqaxqb6qnm73pbohuvqkpxz2zowh57bxqawkid.onion"
]
